<title>USA: J&amp;J anti-epileptic Topamax cleared by FDA.</title>
<headline>J&amp;J anti-epileptic Topamax cleared by FDA.</headline>
<dateline>RARITAN, N.J. 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ortho-McNeil Pharmaceutical, a division of Johnson &amp; Johnson, said that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has granted marketing clearance for Topamax, a new anti-epileptic drug, to reduce the frequency of seizures.</p>
<p>Topamax is indicated as adjunctive therapy for the most common seizure type, partial onset seizures, in adults, the company said.</p>
</text>
